From c242297c94b6dabe1277e4f0aa5adb64a49e5185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:19:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] servers and apps: fix what the static analysis found

- registrar: GetRecentDocuments() and GetRecentFolders() copied the file
  type and signature into 240 byte buffers without a bound -- any
  application could overflow the registrar's heap. Longer ones are refused.
- Deskbar: disabled recents submenus leaked on every open of the Deskbar
  menu, the tray's popup menu leaked when the clock is visible, and each
  team item leaked its name (one per application launch) along with the
  copies that TBarApp::Subscribe() hands out.
- Mail: "MAIL:reply_with" was never used, since ReadAttr() returns the
  number of bytes read, not B_OK.
- debug_server: /dev/dprintf was opened read-only, so its stdout and stderr
  lost everything.
- net_server: rewriting the dynamic part of resolv.conf wrote without
  positioning the stream after reading, and left the rest of a longer
  earlier list behind; the services' pipe was made with pipe(&fReadPipe),
  counting on fWritePipe to follow it in memory (cppcheck).
- login, su, passwd: tty errors were printed to the input stream.
- Deskbar's StatusView and BarView tested (a != x || a != y) and
  (a == NULL && b == NULL) where they meant && and ||.

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/afxtest, registrar-long-type and
text-sniffer (the registrar survives).

